.TH jc 1 2026-11-09 1.26.3 "JSON Convert"
.SH NAME
\fBjc\fP \- JSON Convert JSONifies the output of many CLI tools, file-types,
and strings
.SH SYNOPSIS

Standard syntax:

.RS
COMMAND | \fBjc\fP [SLICE] [OPTIONS] PARSER

cat FILE | \fBjc\fP [SLICE] [OPTIONS] PARSER

echo STRING | \fBjc\fP [SLICE] [OPTIONS] PARSER
.RE

Magic syntax:

.RS
\fBjc\fP [SLICE] [OPTIONS] COMMAND

\fBjc\fP [SLICE] [OPTIONS] /proc/<path-to-procfile>
.RE

.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBjc\fP JSONifies the output of many CLI tools, file-types, and common strings
for easier parsing in scripts. It reads command output, a file, or a string from
\fBSTDIN\fP and writes JSON to \fBSTDOUT\fP. With the "magic" syntax, put
\fBjc\fP and its options in front of the command or \fB/proc\fP file path
instead (command aliases and shell builtins are not supported).

